dims(self: Any, a: Tensor, axis: int) -> Tensor:\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/densitymatrix.py:329:    def expectation(\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/quantum.py:1521:    Generate a local Hamiltonian operator based on the given sequence of Tensor.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/quantum.py:1523:    For large Hilbert space, sparse Hamiltonian is recommended\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/quantum.py:1527:    :param matrix_form: Return Hamiltonian operator in form of matrix, defaults to True.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/quantum.py:1529:    :return: The Hamiltonian operator in form of QuOperator or matrix.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/quantum.py:2136:    Generate Heisenberg Hamiltonian with possible external fields.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/quantum.py:2162:    :param sparse: Whether to return sparse Hamiltonian operator, default is True.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/quantum.py:2167:    :return: Hamiltonian measurements\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/quantum.py:2970:    :param h: Hamiltonian operator in form of Tensor or QuOperator.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/quantum.py:2977:    :return: The free energy of the given density matrix with the Hamiltonian operator.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
